-- ORONA V78: Original integrated Streamer toggle now temporarily hides EVERY
-- Orona ESP layer and private HUD/chat/name elements, restores settings on exit.
-- Right Ctrl toggles Streamer Mode; Right Shift continues to open the menu.
-- V78 standing-pallet repair recognizes NewPallet / case-variant active branches
-- on maps where the original Intact-first selection missed upright geometry.
-- ORONA V77: Standing-pallet repair, Player ESP includes Zombie / Servant NPCs,
-- and background-aware Heartbeat skill-check loop with focus-safe input routing.
-- Previous V76 weapon/parry, menu and all existing gameplay features are preserved.
-- Orona V73: Vault ESP anchored strictly to Window.Bottom; VaultTrigger used only for validation.
-- KITTY VISION ORONA V68 | V4 Moonwalk: camera-relative backward movement, 36 degree body turn / 65% side, flashlight-safe follow
-- V63: Restore V60-style model-shaped Highlight on visible Intact pallet geometry.
-- V63: Never apply the window-only Billboard square to pallets; broken pallets remain hidden.
-- V68: One cute marker per real Window/Vault assembly, anchored at VaultTrigger or inviswall.
-- V64: Do not light ESPs up in lobby; restore only when gameplay is confirmed.
-- V64: More responsive A/D strafing without turning the torso hard or reducing speed.
-- V63: Smooth lateral steering, immediate full-strength move input; retain observed sprint WalkSpeed.
-- V62: direct playable Newpallet.Intact detection, no Highlight slot contention.
-- V62: direct Window/VaultTrigger, inviswall and Bottom marker discovery.
-- V62: no guessed sprint speed; 15-degree body steering instead of 58-degree turn.
-- V61 UI hover glow, gate-ready !, and all unrelated options are preserved.
-- V61: click-hint hover outline for peeking Kitty Tools tab.
-- V61: exit gate ! when unlocked, powered, open, or all generators confirmed completed.
-- V61: moonwalk reinjects sprint after physical Shift release and maintains captured sprint speed.
-- V61: stronger A/D strafing and more responsive body steering.
-- V61: one small flat, camera-facing pink square per usable window.
-- Based on V60; preserves other features and art.
-- Window models with Bottom / VaultTrigger / inviswall now qualify.
-- ESP uses through-wall adornments for windows (avoids the Highlight limit),
-- known folders are indexed immediately, and A/D have more lateral control.
-- Preserves V58 UI, asset art, toggles, keybinds and other gameplay features.
-- Confirmed paths from Roblox Studio Explorer:
-- Map.newGenerators.Generator, Map.resources.Generators (alternate maps),
-- Map.Pallets / Map.resources.Pallets, Map.resources.Windows.Window.Bottom,
-- Map.ESCAPEGATE.ESCAPEGATE.Gate.ExitLever.
-- Dropped pallets REMAIN visible; only destroyed/broken/removed ones disappear.
-- Kitty Vision Orona V55 | Menu art is separate from click controls; active-map objective detection.
-- KITTY VISION / ORONA V54 — TWO DISTINCT ANIME CATGIRL ICONS & POLISHED UI
-- KITTY VISION / ORONA V53 — COUTURE UI — based on working V52 gameplay code
-- ORONA V52: V51 gameplay base, ornate playable UI, persistent player highlights, lobby-safe vault scans.
-- ORONA V56:  V49 base; more reliable multi-map Vault ESP, upgraded catgirl UI,
-- lower-impact pumpkins, anime sleeping/awake status, fullbody clipping fix.
-- V47: Pumpkin ESP, torso-only Gun Aimlock, expanded Vault ESP and lower scan load.
-- Uses real gameplay attributes and prompt evidence where available; falls
-- back to conservative map model signatures when game has custom prompts.
-- Preserves Player ESP, Moonwalk, Flashlight Aimlock, Pallets and existing features.
